From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi: sun55i-pck600: Set the controller of each
 domain

Nothing sets pd->pck, which sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power() dereferences to
report a domain that fails to change state, so such a failure oopses
instead of being reported. Set it in the probe loop.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with the A733 node;
all eleven domains register without an oops. The error path itself was
not triggered.

Fixes: 76e4310115ca ("pmdomain: sunxi: add driver for Allwinner A523's PCK-600 power controller")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
index 8a37d11b65a2..6d34101794d1 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -176,6 +176,7 @@ static int sunxi_pck600_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		pd->genpd.power_on = sunxi_pck600_power_on;
 		pd->genpd.flags = pd_desc->flags;
 		pd->base = base + PPU_REG_SIZE * i;
+		pd->pck = pck;
 
 		sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(pd, desc);
 		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false);
